{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_5hpciilmdsdr7vcy2djpgnoywuvrk3cddqkobcoyp5rjoyysnp5a","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Verification complete. **99 tests, 0 failures.** The Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n- **`SYMBOLS.md`** — C `.so` exports 39 symbols, Rust `.so` exports 39. Diff empty both directions; 0 non-libc undefined symbols. No missing modules, no stubs needed.\n- **Phase B** — all 60 `CONFIGS.md` rows pass across thousands of fixed-seed randomized inputs per row.\n- **Binary** — N/A. `CMakeLists.txt` has no `add_executable`, `Cargo.toml` no `[[bin]]`.\n- **Phase C** — all 42 `ERRORS.md` rows have a passing differential test asserting the *specific* sentinel (exactly `0`, exactly `+0.0`, exactly `c2V(0,0)`), not just \"both failed\".\n- **Feature combos** — `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; `check_features.sh` confirms default and `--no-default-features` both pass.\n\n## Two real problems found and fixed (both in the test harness, not the translation)\n\n**1. `cargo test` was testing a stale `.so`.** This crate's only lib target is a `cdylib`, and **cargo does not build a cdylib-only lib target for `cargo test`** — integration tests have no rlib to link. So bare `cargo test` loaded whatever `.so` a previous `cargo build` left behind, silently turning every assertion into a no-op. Confirmed by touching `src/lib.rs`: the `.so` stayed byte-identical and older than the source. Fixed with `run_tests.sh` (builds both libs first) plus a hard `STALE Rust cdylib` panic in the harness as a backstop.\n\n**2. The suite couldn't prove it was able to fail.** All 99 tests passed on the first run, which is exactly when a harness deserves suspicion. Mutation testing with two single-character changes (`c2D`'s `> 0.0` → `>= 0.0`; `c2CircletoCircle`'s `d2 < r2` → `<= r2`) made 13 rows fail across all 4 levels, then pass again after reverting.\n\n## One deliberate comparison relaxation\n\n`f32` comparison is bit-exact **except** that two NaNs count as equal when sign/payload differ. When both SSE operands are NaN the hardware propagates the *destination* register's payload, so the result's sign bit depends purely on register allocation — gcc `-O2` and rustc `-O3` make different but equally valid choices for `a.x*b.x + a.y*b.y`. This was the only divergence in the exercise (in `c2Dot`, `c2Det2`, `c2Mulrv`, only with `-NaN` inputs). `±0.0`, `±inf`, NaN-vs-non-NaN and all finite values stay strict.\n\n## Two rows intentionally not asserted for equality\n\n`ptr_from_parts` and `c2GJK` with an out-of-range enum both hit C **indeterminate** behavior — the former falls off the end of a non-`void` function, the latter leaves `c2Proxy` uninitialized on the stack. Demanding byte-identical output would mean asserting on UB. Instead I pinned down what *is* defined: no crash, `*iterations` stays in `[0,20]`, and the sole reachable-through-public-API consequence (`c2Collided`/`omni_collide` returning `0` *before* dereferencing) is asserted exactly. I did not fabricate agreement on the garbage values.\n\n`src/lib.rs` needed no changes — it compiled clean and was already correct, including faithful reproduction of the C's quirks (untouched proxy on unknown type, `break`-before-`++s.count`, unvalidated negative radii and inverted AABBs)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":734,"cache_read_input_tokens":169402,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":734,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0773ef77-31e4-4429-aef6-a43f46cd5fce","uuid":"df208b40-9ff4-421a-843e-daad3c62dabd","timestamp":"2026-09-05T09:19:04.317Z"}
